  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 5.1. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to identify current skills mismatches and anticipate future skill needs</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pilot implementation of rapid assessment for reskilling and upskilling needs is currently being undertaken in Thailand. The Department of Skills Development (DSD) expanded the coverage of the assessment from one to five sectors as a critical input for national efforts on reskilling and upskilling for the employment recovery from the pandemic and beyond.

Recommendations on evidence based policy were issued to help the Ministry of Labour handle unemployment caused by COVID-19 and automation. ILO shared the Guidelines on Rapid Assessment of reskilling and upskilling needs in response to the COVID-19 crisis that includes questionnaires that were adapted for use in Thailand.

ILO funds this tripartite effort through the implementation of the &quot;Women in STEM Workforce Readiness and Development Program&quot;

ILO provided technical support to strengthen institutional resources and capacities for effective labour policies handling impact of COVID-19 and digital transformation.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">5.1.1. Number of member States that have applied ILO approaches to measure skills mismatches and/or anticipate future skill needs at national and/or sectoral level</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
